(vector (map (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607113500-kotobase-net-ingestion-cloud-itonami-lei"), (:consequences "{:closes \"ADR-2607072300's 'no ingestion pipeline code written' gap, for the\\n            cloud-itonami-lei-* family specifically -- the general 'every actor adopts\\n            this pattern' migration remains open, unchanged from that ADR's own scoping\", :proves \"kotobase.net (via backend.kotobase.net, the apex's real xrpc proxy target\\n             since the 2026-07-08 cutover) is a genuinely operational write/read surface,\\n             demonstrated with real data, not just a design on paper\", :apex-note \"https://kotobase.net apex serves a marketing page at / and returns 404 at\\n               /_health (its own routes, not proxied) -- only /xrpc/* is proxied to\\n               backend.kotobase.net per KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL; this script hits\\n               backend.kotobase.net directly to avoid depending on that proxy's exact\\n               behavior for non-xrpc paths\", :follow-up-needed \"persist the ingestion identity's secret key to a durable store\\n                       (1Password gftdcojp vault or kagi, matching other actors'\\n                       convention) before this session's local environment is lost --\\n                       explicitly NOT done in this ADR\", :re-run-behavior \"re-running the script for newly-added cloud-itonami-lei-* companies\\n                      (ADR-2607110300's rollout is ongoing) will ingest only the new ones\\n                      idempotently; there is no automatic trigger -- manual re-run, or a\\n                      future webhook/west-update-hook extension, out of this ADR's scope\"}"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:problem "{:source \"follow-up to ADR-2607110300: implement the kotobase.net ingestion job\\n            ADR-2607072300 explicitly left unimplemented, using the real\\n            cloud-itonami-lei-* corpus (105 real company ToS repos) as the concrete input\", :investigated [\"kotobase-peer (orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer) is a server-side library, not a\\n     deployed endpoint -- its README example tx-data shape ([:db/add e a v] vectors /\\n     {:s :p :o} maps) is its OWN in-process API, not necessarily the wire format any\\n     deployed XRPC server accepts\" \"the real production kotobase.net write/read surface is\\n     kotoba-lang/kotobase-server's handler.cljc, deployed via\\n     gftdcojp/net-kotobase/kotobase-cf-wasm at https://backend.kotobase.net (apex\\n     https://kotobase.net proxies /xrpc/* there per its own KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL var,\\n     confirmed live since 2026-07-08 per that repo's DEPLOY.md)\" \"kotobase-cf-wasm/wrangler.jsonc's production KOTOBASE_OPERATOR_DIDS var is empty\\n     (open allowlist) -- any self-minted CACAO whose issuer DID equals the graph owner\\n     can transact, no static pre-registration needed, confirmed by reading the actual\\n     deployed config, not assumed\" \"kotoba-lang/kotobase-client already has a complete, tested CACAO/transact/q/datoms\\n     client (src/kotobase/{client,cacao,cid}.cljs) matching the apex's exact auth shape\\n     (kotobase:pin capability + issuer-DID graph scope) -- confirmed runnable directly\\n     under nbb (no shadow-cljs compile step needed) by requiring it with --classpath\" \"first real transact attempt with [:db/add e a v] tx-data failed 400 InternalError\\n     with no detail via the apex; the same request against backend.kotobase.net directly\\n     surfaced 'kotobase: unrecognized tx_edn item', which led to reading\\n     kotobase-server's handler.cljc directly and finding tx-edn->quads only accepts\\n     entity maps (or [:db/retract ...]/[:db/retractEntity ...]), not [:db/add ...]\"], :risk \"assuming kotobase-peer's README example shape was the real wire format (without\\n          reading the actual server-side parser) would have produced a script that always\\n          400s in production while looking correct in isolation\"}"), (:adr/body "\n# ADR-2607113500: kotobase.net ingestion fold job for cloud-itonami-lei-* actors\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-11\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (+ Claude, オーナー承認のうえ実行)\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2607072300 が決めたのは「actorの公開データは自身のgit repo内のEDN quad-log\n(`80-data/public/*.journal.edn`) が正本、kotobase.net はそこから畳み込む派生インデックス」\nという一般設計であり、同ADR自身の `:not-decided` は「取り込みパイプライン\n（journal → kotobase-peer fold job）のコードは書いていない」「trigger mechanism\n（west update hook / GitHub webhook / kotobase.net pull）は未定」と明記していた。\n\n本セッションで ADR-2607110300（cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog）により、\n実在企業105社分の `80-data/public/tos.journal.edn`（実ToS全文 + 出典URL + 取得日時 +\nsha256）を持つ公開リポジトリ群が既に存在する状態になった——これが\nADR-2607072300の欠けていたパイプラインを実装するための、具体的で現実の入力集合を\n初めて提供した。\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. トリガー機構: pull-based batch fold job（webhookでもwest hookでもない）\n\n対象は「既に存在する105個の静的リポジトリ」であり、継続的に変化するライブストリーム\nではないため、最もシンプルで正しい選択は **pull型のバッチ fold job**——GitHub org を\nenumerate し、各リポジトリの `blueprint.edn` + `tos.journal.edn` を Contents API\n（`raw.githubusercontent.com`、認証不要、public repoのため）経由で取得し、\nkotobase.net へ transact するスクリプト。webhook/west-update-hookは「継続的に増える\nアクター」向けの将来の拡張として残す（本ADRでは実装しない、ADR-2607072300自身の\n\"not-decided\" と同じ扱い）。\n\n### 2. 実装: 実 nbb + 実 cljs、既存の `kotobase-client` をそのまま再利用\n\n`scripts/kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei.cljs`（root CLAUDE.mdのruntime優先順位に\n従い、フルのDatalogエンジンはcljsネイティブなホスト実行環境がまだ無いため\n（`kotobase-cf-wasm/DEPLOY.md` 実測）、nbbで実cljsソースをそのまま動かすのが現状\n正しい選択——`kotoba-lang/kotobase-client` の `kotobase.client`/`kotobase.cacao`/\n`kotobase.cid` を **一切書き直さず** `--classpath` 経由でそのまま require\n（nbb実行で動作確認済み、shadow-cljsのコンパイルステップ不要）。CACAO発行・\ndid:key導出・SIWEメッセージ構築・DAG-CBORエンコードは全て既存実装をそのまま使う\n——認証まわりを新規に書かない。\n\n### 3. アイデンティティ: 本ジョブ専用の新規 self-sovereign actor identity\n\n新規 Ed25519 鍵を生成し、`did:key:z6Mkh6mnYrfXNjDSoRQfRK9a2QanvaSAVAqDFK44Vpss5ZSA`\nとして自己発行。秘密鍵は `scripts/.kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei-identity.hex`\n（`scripts/.gitignore` で除外、gitに一切コミットしない——root CLAUDE.mdの秘密鍵\n取り扱い規律と同じ）。グラフは この DID 由来の\n`kotobase/db/<did>/cloud-itonami-lei-catalog`\n（graph CID: `bafyreifq6p445b472n6qbutttfaa3fegq5bbjnnxcmrogi5y6ksw46qwty`）——\nオペレータの許可リスト（`KOTOBASE_OPERATOR_DIDS`）は本番で空（open、誰でも\n自分のgraphへtransact可能、`kotobase-cf-wasm/wrangler.jsonc` で実測確認）なので、\n静的な事前登録は不要だった。**この鍵ファイルを失うと、再実行が新しい別グラフを\n始めてしまい今回のデータへ継続できなくなる**——現状ローカルのみに存在し、\n1Password/kagiへの複製は本ADRの範囲外のフォローアップとして明記する（正直な\n未完了事項——他actorの秘密鍵管理の慣例に倣うなら本来はkagi/1Password登録が\n望ましいが、本セッションでは行っていない）。\n\n### 4. 発見した実際のwireフォーマット（ADRの想定と実装時の食い違い）\n\nADR-2607072300 のプロトタイプ的な記述は kotobase-peer の README 例\n（`[:db/add e a v]` ベクタ形式）を踏襲していたが、**実際に本番 `backend.kotobase.net`\nへ POST したところ `400 {\"ok\":false,\"error\":\"InternalError\"}`**（詳細メッセージ無し）\nで失敗した。`kotoba-lang/kotobase-server` の `handler.cljc`（`tx-edn->quads`）を\n直接読んだところ、`tx_edn` が受理するのは **エンティティmapのベクタ**\n`[{:db/id \"e\" :ns/attr v ...} ...]` であり、ベクタ形式が許されるのは\n`[:db/retract e a v]`（4要素）と `[:db/retractEntity e]`（2要素）の2種類のみ\n——`[:db/add e a v]` は`tx-edn->quads`の`cond`に一致せず\n`\"kotobase: unrecognized tx_edn item\"`で例外になる（`backend.kotobase.net`への\n直接POSTで実際にこのメッセージを確認）。エンティティmap形式に修正した後、\ntransactは`{\"ok\":true,...}`で成功した。**この食い違いはコードを読んで実測で\n確認したものであり、ADR文面の想定を鵜呑みにしなかった結果発見できた。**\n\n### 5. 実行結果（実データ、実105社）\n\n`gh api \"orgs/cloud-itonami/repos?...\" --paginate`（`gh repo list` のGraphQL経路は\n本セッション中にレート制限を使い切ったため、REST経路に切替——別quotaで同じ結果を\n取得できる）で列挙した **105社全リポジトリを実際にtransact、105/105成功、\n失敗ゼロ**。各社: `:company/*`（blueprint.edn由来）+ 各ToS文書ごとの\n`:tos/full-text`/`:tos/source-url`/`:tos/retrieved-at`/`:tos/sha256`/\n`:tos/doc-type`（tos.journal.edn由来、`:tos/company`で親エンティティへ逆参照）。\n\n**冪等性を実測確認**: ExxonMobilエンティティ（`lei:J3WHBG0MTS7O8ZVMDC91`）を\n2回transactした後も `:eavt` のdatom数は6件のまま（12件へ倍増しない）——\n`:db/id`をキーにしたcardinality-one upsertとして機能することを実際のserver応答で\n確認した（理論上そうなるはず、ではなく実測）。\n\n**読み出し確認（`q`, 実multi-clause Datalog join）**:\n```\n{:find [?name ?url] :where [[?e :company/lei \"J3WHBG0MTS7O8ZVMDC91\"]\n                             [?e :company/legal-name ?name]\n                             [?tos :tos/company ?e]\n                             [?tos :tos/source-url ?url]]}\n=> [[\"Exxon Mobil Corporation\" \"https://corporate.exxonmobil.com/global-legal-pages/terms-and-conditions\"]]\n```\n実際の本番 `ai.gftd.apps.kotobase.datomic.q` エンドポイントへの実POSTで、\n実際にjoinされた行が返ることを確認した。\n\n## Consequences\n\n- ADR-2607072300 の「取り込みパイプライン未実装」という欠落を、\n  cloud-itonami-lei-* ファミリーについてのみ実際に埋めた——一般則\n  （「全actorがこのpatternを採用する」移行）は依然として同ADRのまま未着手。\n- `kotobase.net`（`https://backend.kotobase.net` 経由。apexの `https://kotobase.net`\n  自体は `/`・`/_health` はマーケティングページを返す独自ルートを持ち、\n  `/xrpc/*` のみ `KOTOBA_BACKEND_URL` 経由でproxyする構成——本スクリプトは\n  proxyの不確実性を避けてbackend直叩きにした）が、実際に運用可能な\n  書き込み/読み出し面であることを実データで証明した。\n- 秘密鍵がローカルファイルのみに存在し、1Password/kagi等の永続化された\n  vaultに未登録——**このセッション環境を離れると鍵を喪失するリスクがある**。\n  次回このジョブを再実行する前に、鍵の永続化（他actorの慣例に倣うなら\n  1Password `gftdcojp` vault か kagi）をフォローアップとして行うことを推奨する。\n- 新規companyが `cloud-itonami-lei-*` ファミリーに追加されるたび\n  （ADR-2607110300のロールアウトは継続中）、このスクリプトを再実行すれば\n  追加分だけ取り込まれる（既存分は冪等に無変化）——ただし自動トリガーは無い\n  （手動再実行、または将来のwebhook/west-update-hook拡張が必要、本ADRの\n  スコープ外）。\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **push型webhook（各cloud-itonami-lei-*リポジトリのpushで即時transact）** —\n  却下（今回は見送り、将来検討）。105個の静的リポジトリに対して常時稼働の\n  webhookリスナーを立てるインフラコストは、バッチジョブの手動/定期再実行に\n  見合わない。継続的に成長するactorファミリーには適するため、\n  ADR-2607072300の\"not-decided\"のまま将来のフォローアップとして残す。\n- **kotobase-peer の直接組み込み（in-process `commit!`）** — 却下。\n  `kotobase-peer` はサーバサイドのライブラリで、R2/B2バックエンド配線・\n  CACAO検証・IPNS head署名は `kotobase-cf-wasm`/`kotobase-server` 側の責務\n  ——このジョブはXRPCクライアントとして振る舞うのが正しい層で、\n  エンジンを直接埋め込む理由がない。\n- **shadow-cljsでコンパイルしたNode bundle** — 却下（今回は）。nbbで\n  `kotobase-client` の実cljsソースをそのまま動かせることを実測確認できたため、\n  ビルドステップを追加する理由がなかった。将来この方式が壊れた場合の\n  フォールバックとして記録しておく。\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607072300（actor-public-data-git-journal-kotobase-index）— 本ADRが\n  閉じる\"not-decided\"項目の出典。\n- ADR-2607110300（cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog）— 取り込み対象の\n  journal/blueprintスキーマの出典。\n- `kotoba-lang/kotobase-client`（`src/kotobase/{client,cacao,cid}.cljs`）—\n  本ジョブが再利用したCACAO/XRPCクライアント実装、無改変。\n- `kotoba-lang/kotobase-server`（`src/kotobase/server/handler.cljc`）—\n  実際のtx_edn wireフォーマット（`tx-edn->quads`）の一次情報源。\n- `gftdcojp/net-kotobase/kotobase-cf-wasm/DEPLOY.md` — production cutover\n  (2026-07-08) の実配線と `KOTOBASE_OPERATOR_DIDS` の空許可リスト設定の出典。"), (:alternatives "[{:option \"push-based webhook per cloud-itonami-lei-* repo\", :rejected_because \"infrastructure cost of a standing webhook listener isn't justified\\n                        for 105 static, already-existing repos; left as future work for\\n                        continuously-growing actor families, matching ADR-2607072300's own\\n                        not-decided deferral\"} {:option \"embed kotobase-peer's engine in-process (direct commit! calls) instead of\\n             going through the XRPC client\", :rejected_because \"kotobase-peer is a server-side library whose R2/B2 storage wiring,\\n                        CACAO verification, and IPNS head signing live in\\n                        kotobase-cf-wasm/kotobase-server -- this job is correctly an XRPC\\n                        client, not a second engine deployment\"} {:option \"compile a Node bundle via shadow-cljs instead of running via nbb\", :rejected_because \"empirically confirmed kotobase-client's real .cljs source runs\\n                        directly under nbb via --classpath with no compile step -- adding\\n                        a build pipeline had no justification once that was proven\"}]"), (:db/id -1), (:decision "{:trigger-mechanism {:choice \"pull-based batch fold job\", :why \"the 105 cloud-itonami-lei-* repos are a static, already-existing set, not a live\\n          continuously-changing stream -- a script enumerating the org and fetching each\\n          repo's blueprint.edn + 80-data/public/tos.journal.edn via\\n          raw.githubusercontent.com (public repos, no auth needed) is simpler and correct\\n          for this shape; webhook/west-update-hook triggers are left as future work for\\n          actor families that grow continuously, matching ADR-2607072300's own deferral\"}, :implementation {:script \"scripts/kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei.cljs\", :runtime \"nbb running real .cljs source (no shadow-cljs compile step) -- per root\\n              CLAUDE.md's runtime priority, a full Datalog engine has no cljs-native\\n              hosting runtime yet (kotobase-cf-wasm/DEPLOY.md's own finding), so nbb\\n              running real cljs is the correct current choice for this class of script\", :reuse \"requires kotoba-lang/kotobase-client's kotobase.client/kotobase.cacao/\\n            kotobase.cid verbatim via --classpath -- CACAO minting, did:key derivation,\\n            SIWE message construction, DAG-CBOR encoding are ALL reused unmodified, not\\n            reimplemented\", :repo-enumeration \"gh api \\\"orgs/cloud-itonami/repos\\\" --paginate (REST), not gh repo\\n                        list (GraphQL) -- GraphQL's session-wide rate limit was exhausted\\n                        mid-development by this session's earlier isic-family rollout;\\n                        REST has its own separate, much larger budget\"}, :identity {:did \"did:key:z6Mkh6mnYrfXNjDSoRQfRK9a2QanvaSAVAqDFK44Vpss5ZSA\", :graph_cid \"bafyreifq6p445b472n6qbutttfaa3fegq5bbjnnxcmrogi5y6ksw46qwty\", :db_name \"cloud-itonami-lei-catalog\", :secret-storage \"scripts/.kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei-identity.hex, gitignored\\n                      via scripts/.gitignore, never committed -- same discipline as every\\n                      other actor's .<actor>/identity.edn per root CLAUDE.md\", :operator-allowlist \"empty/open in production (KOTOBASE_OPERATOR_DIDS=\\\"\\\" in\\n                          kotobase-cf-wasm/wrangler.jsonc) -- no static pre-registration\\n                          needed, self-sovereign per the existing CACAO actor pattern\", :known-gap \"the secret key exists ONLY as a local file in this session's environment\\n                -- not yet mirrored to 1Password/kagi like other actors' secrets\\n                typically are; losing this file before a future re-run would orphan a new,\\n                empty graph instead of continuing this one. Flagged as an honest follow-up,\\n                not resolved in this ADR.\"}, :wire-format-correction {:wrong \"[:db/add e a v] vectors (kotobase-peer's own in-process README example shape)\", :right \"a vector of entity maps [{:db/id \\\"e\\\" :ns/attr v ...} ...] -- the ONLY other\\n            accepted vector forms are [:db/retract e a v] (4-elem) and\\n            [:db/retractEntity e] (2-elem), per kotobase-server's handler.cljc\\n            tx-edn->quads dispatch, read directly from source, not inferred\", :evidence \"first attempt: POST https://backend.kotobase.net/xrpc/....transact with\\n               [:db/add e a v] tx_edn -> 400 {\\\"error\\\":\\\"InternalError\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\n               \\\"kotobase: unrecognized tx_edn item\\\"}. Corrected attempt with entity-map\\n               tx_edn -> 200 {\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"commit\\\":\\\"bafyreif...\\\",\\\"datom_count\\\":1}\"}, :execution-result {:companies-attempted 105, :companies-succeeded 105, :companies-failed 0, :per-company-facts [\"blueprint.edn fields (:company/legal-name/:lei/:jurisdiction/\\n                          :website/:ticker) + :company/repo, on entity lei:<LEI>\" \"one entity per distinct ToS doc-id in tos.journal.edn, carrying\\n                          :tos/full-text/:tos/source-url/:tos/retrieved-at/:tos/sha256/\\n                          :tos/doc-type + a :tos/company back-reference\"], :idempotency-verification \"re-transacted ExxonMobil's entity (lei:J3WHBG0MTS7O8ZVMDC91)\\n                                a second time; :eavt datom count for that entity stayed at\\n                                6 (not doubled to 12) -- confirmed via a real datoms call\\n                                after the re-transact, not assumed from cardinality-one\\n                                semantics alone\", :read-verification \"real multi-clause Datalog q against production:\\n                         {:find [?name ?url] :where [[?e :company/lei\\n                         \\\"J3WHBG0MTS7O8ZVMDC91\\\"] [?e :company/legal-name ?name]\\n                         [?tos :tos/company ?e] [?tos :tos/source-url ?url]]} returned\\n                         [[\\\"Exxon Mobil Corporation\\\"\\n                         \\\"https://corporate.exxonmobil.com/global-legal-pages/terms-and-conditions\\\"]]\\n                         -- a real join across two entity types round-tripped correctly\"}}"), (:frontmatter "{:authoritative_for [\"For the cloud-itonami-lei-* actor family (ADR-2607110300), ADR-2607072300's open\\n     'journal -> kotobase-peer fold job' item is closed by a pull-based batch fold job\\n     (scripts/kotobase-ingest-cloud-itonami-lei.cljs, real nbb+cljs reusing\\n     kotoba-lang/kotobase-client verbatim), not a push-based webhook or a west-update hook\" \"kotobase.net's real production XRPC tx_edn wire format is a vector of ENTITY MAPS\\n     [{:db/id \\\"e\\\" :ns/attr v ...} ...], not [:db/add e a v] triples -- the latter is\\n     kotobase-peer's own in-process API shape (its README), not what kotobase-server's\\n     handler.cljc/tx-edn->quads accepts over the wire; discovered empirically via a real\\n     400 'kotobase: unrecognized tx_edn item' response, not assumed from ADR prose\" \"Idempotent re-ingestion is achieved by keyed cardinality-one upsert (same :db/id +\\n     attrs re-asserted), empirically verified (re-transacting one company left its :eavt\\n     datom count unchanged, not doubled)\" \"All 105 cloud-itonami-lei-* companies existing at ingestion time are live-queryable in\\n     kotobase.net today via a real multi-clause Datalog join, verified end to end\" \"The general 'every actor adopts the 80-data/public/*.journal.edn -> kotobase.net\\n     pattern' migration remains open exactly as ADR-2607072300 scoped it -- this ADR closes\\n     the gap for ONE actor family, not the general case\"], :authoritative true, :superseded_by [], :topic \"kotobase-net-ingestion-cloud-itonami-lei\", :related [\"90-docs/adr/2607072300-actor-public-data-git-journal-kotobase-index.edn\" \"90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn\" \"orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-client\" \"orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer\" \"orgs/gftdcojp/net-kotobase/kotobase-cf-wasm/DEPLOY.md\"], :title \"ADR-2607113500: kotobase.net ingestion fold job for cloud-itonami-lei-* -- closes ADR-2607072300's open trigger-mechanism gap for this actor family\", :status \"accepted\", :supersedes [], :id \"adr-2607113500-kotobase-net-ingestion-cloud-itonami-lei\", :last_verified \"2026-07-11\", :doc_type \"adr\"}"), (:adr/title "ADR-2607113500: kotobase.net ingestion fold job for cloud-itonami-lei-* — closes ADR-2607072300's open trigger-mechanism gap for this actor family"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))